      {
        "id": "s1",
        "title": {
          "en": "The neuter branch",
          "hi": "नपुंसक शाखा"
        },
        "image": {
          "id": "nf1-phala-s1",
          "brief": "The tree of green mist in the library with a second lower branch hung with a different set of leaf-tags, Dādī pointing to it with her pen and comparing it to the upper branch; Śuka on a shelf pulling at a tag.",
          "alt": {
            "en": "A tree of name-tags with two branches, one pointing to the other",
            "hi": "दो शाखाओं वाला नाम-पत्तों का पेड़, एक शाखा की ओर इशारा"
          },
          "text_in_image": [],
          "ratio": "4:3",
          "cast": [
            "you",
            "dadi",
            "shuka",
            "acarya",
            "vrikshaka"
          ],
          "place": "pathashala"
        },
        "depth": "core",
        "skills": [],
        "sutras": [],
        "kind": "story",
        "narration": {
          "en": "On a lower branch of the green tree hangs a second set of leaf-tags, close to the first but a little different. “Neuters,” says Dādī. “Almost the same as the masculines. The family resemblance is strong, and only a few places differ.” Vṛkṣaka shakes a branch and the tags rustle, delighted.",
          "hi": "हरे पेड़ की एक नीची शाखा पर पत्ते-टैगों का दूसरा समूह लटका है, पहले के क़रीब पर थोड़ा अलग। “नपुंसक,” दादी कहती हैं। “पुंलिंग से लगभग वही। पारिवारिक समानता गहरी है, बस कुछ जगहों पर अन्तर है।” वृक्षक एक शाखा हिलाता है और टैग ख़ुशी से सरसराते हैं।"
        },
        "lines": [],
        "quote": null
      },
